# Portfolio site

Interactive portfolio for Daniel A Rodrigues. One shared content source in TypeScript. The live site is a static Vite SPA: home plus `/projects/:slug`. There is no assistant overlay and no API.

## Stack

- Vite, React 19, React Router, TypeScript (strict)
- Tailwind (`surface-*` CSS variables, dark `color-scheme`, sage `glow` accent)
- Fonts: Geist (body) + Instrument Serif (`--font-display`) + JetBrains Mono (`--font-mono`)
- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`
- GitHub Pages via `.github/workflows/pages.yml` on `main`. Vite `base` is `/` locally and in the Pages build (`VITE_BASE` / `VITE_SITE_URL` can override). Public files go through `publicUrl()` in `@src/lib/publicUrl.ts`.

## Layout

- Entry: `index.html` → `@src/main.tsx` → `BrowserRouter` (`basename={import.meta.env.BASE_URL}`) → `@src/App.tsx`
- Shell: `@src/components/app-shell.tsx` wraps every route with `ThemeBackground` and `Navbar`
- Home (`@src/pages/home.tsx`): `Hero` → `ExperienceTimeline` (`#experience`) → `ProjectsSection` (`#projects`, personal only) → `SkillsGrid` → `AboutSection` → `OutsideWork` → `ContactSection`
- Project routes: `@src/pages/project-detail.tsx` at `/projects/:slug` from `PROJECTS`. Work projects still list under the owning role in `ExperienceTimeline`. `npm run build` copies `index.html` to `dist/projects/<slug>/index.html` and `dist/404.html`
- Contact (email/GitHub/LinkedIn/resume) lives in `ContactSection` (`#contact`), not a global footer
- UI: `@src/components/ui/`

## Content

- `@src/shared/profile.ts` (profile, experience, skills, interests, education, nav)
- `@src/shared/projects.ts` (`PROJECTS`, `PERSONAL_PROJECTS`, `getProjectBySlug`, `getProjectsByExperienceId`, `origin: "work" | "personal"`)
- Archived for a later assistant: `@src/server/ai/systemPrompt.ts`, `@src/server/ai/context.ts`, `@src/lib/contactCta.ts`. The Vite client must not import the prompt modules
- Resume is `public/resume.pdf`. Prefix with `publicUrl()`

## Theming

- Single dark look via `html.dark` and tokens in `@src/styles/globals.css`
- Use `surface-*` and `glow`. Never hardcode `zinc-*` or raw hex
- Editorial style: hairline dividers, `font-display` headings, mono for tech/metadata

## Guardrails

- Do not add Route Handlers, Mongo, OpenRouter, or a chat overlay unless explicitly requested
- Skill logos live in `@src/shared/skillIcons.ts` if icons come back. Never `import { … } from 'simple-icons'`
- Unit tests go under `tests/` mirroring `src/`
- After a large feature or layout change, update `.cursor/rules/` in the same PR (`sync-cursor-rules`)
